# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites files to
# CRLF on disk while git stores LF. Two things then break:
#
#   1. `prettier --check` uses `endOfLine: "lf"`, so it fails locally on files
#      that are perfectly fine in CI — or passes locally and fails in CI.
#   2. `git diff` reports every line of every file as changed, which buries
#      real changes and makes review useless.
#
# The runtime targets (Linux containers, GitHub Actions) are LF-only, so LF
# everywhere is also what actually ships.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never transformed, never diffed as text.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Marked so GitHub collapses it in review and diffs stay readable.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
